<title>UK: Fitness First shares set first-day premium.</title>
<headline>Fitness First shares set first-day premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Fitness First Plc set a 13 percent premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The shares were marked up at 90-1/2p by 0835 GMT, after being placed at 80p, though no trades were recorded in the stock. The float valued the health and fitness club operator at 22.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Fitness First Plc was established in 1992 and runs six health clubs. It plans to expand its chain to over 25 in the next three years.</p>
<p>The broker to the flotation was Henderson Crosthwaite.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
